### I. ARCHITECTURAL EXPLANATION & ENGINEERING RATIONALE

The audit confirms a systemic vulnerability in the intersection of physics, infrastructure geometry, and civic governance during galvanic/telemetric severance ("Black-Sky conditions"):

1. **Non-Linear Fluid Dynamics vs. Linear Legal Fiction (Art. 3.6.2, Art. 6.1.3):**  
   The previous canonical formulation prescribed a uniform proportional ("pro-rata") volumetric throttling during catastrophic supply deficits. Under the Darcy-Weisbach formulation, frictional head loss varies quadratically with flow velocity. Continuous proportional throttling causes the hydraulic grade line (HGL) to drop below the physical elevations of crest-line nodes, inducing vapor cavity formation, siphon fracture, and complete de-watering of high-elevation communes, while low-elevation basins maintain hydraulic head. This differential access violates the non-derogable baseline of human flourishing (Article 1.3).  
   *Remedy:* The amendment formally abolishes continuous proportional throttling across pressurized distribution conduits. In its place, it mandates **discrete, pulsed batch-cycled head-retention dispatch**—delivering water at full operational velocity and dynamic head during synchronized operational windows—interleaved with zero-flow pressure retention, supported by passive, non-electric break-pressure balance cisterns.

2. **Benthic Particulate Ingestion at Reservoir Terminals (Art. 4.4.4):**  
   Intakes anchored at or near the reservoir invert draw high concentrations of benthic sediments, anaerobic decomposition byproducts, and mobilized heavy-particulate pathogens during extended unpowered drawdowns.  
   *Remedy:* Mandates that all municipal Tier 1 potable intakes utilize **passively articulating, floating subsurface decanters** tethered within the limnological sweet zone (above benthic sediment layers and below surface photic algae zones), coupled with mechanical fail-safe scouring flumes operated strictly by gravity and head differentials.

3. **Sortition Coordination Latency & Hydraulic Asynchrony (Art. 6.5.4, Art. 7.1.4):**  
   During complete black-sky communications severance, autonomous three-citizen sortition panels operating with localized emergency authority can execute unsynchronized manual bypass actuations. In a shared hydraulic basin, an upstream panel opening an uncoordinated bypass immediately collapses downstream siphon loops and reservoir balance.  
   *Remedy:* Sortition emergency discretion is bounded by physical invariant: civic override panels are prohibited from actuating bypasses outside of pre-calibrated, ephemeris-synchronized temporal distribution windows (Solar Noon / Solar Midnight cycles) and are constrained by mechanical, hydromechanically coupled interlocks that physically prevent upstream gate overrides without downstream hydrostatic counter-pressure verification.

